1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:08,340
Slide 38 clarifies the most important governance distinction in modern AI: Human-IN-the-Loop versus Human-ON-the-Loop.

2
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:21,500
In the old Human-IN-the-loop model on the left, the human had to click "Approve" on every single micro-step. It created a massive bottleneck and completely exhausted the user!

3
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:39,910
But on the right, we implement Human-ON-the-loop (HOTL). The swarm executes inside pre-approved guardrail boundaries. The human acts like an air traffic controller—monitoring the dashboard, setting the flight plans, and only intervening when an anomaly or exception arises.

4
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:49,030
This is how you achieve massive scale without burning yourself out. Strategic oversight over micromanagement.

